  biomeName: Sea-Stack Forest
  minDepthMeters: 0
  maxDepthMeters: 300
  shortDescription: A forest of isolated circular stone pillars over coral dust and
    shell fields.
  isPlaceholder: 0
  visitPurpose: Early exploration biome. Come here to learn routes, gather basics,
    and follow strong natural shapes and search obvious pockets.
  commonRewardHook: Common runs pay out in Fiber Kelp and Membrane Tissue.
  rareRewardHook: 'Rare pull is modest: Biolum Paste and Fiber Mesh.'
  landmarkIdentity: Sea-Stack Forest reads through spires, steps, and big natural
    crowns. Landmarks should feel bright and readable.
  safePocketIdentity: Safe pockets are frequent. The player should often see a clear
    reset point nearby.
  riskSummary: 'Main failure mode: bad drops and exposed lines. Creature pressure
    stays medium.'
  extractionFocus: 'Mixed salvage, harvest pockets, and risky reef-node peels. Early
    tier: keep runs short and favor stone pockets and hard-form nodes.'
  landmarkGuidance: Dominant landmark is reef crown or porous fossil wall. This slot
    should read through coral windows and rib-like skeletons; use vertical forms
    to keep heading.
